## 3. Equity and Compensation Analysis

A core component of our commitment to equity is ensuring fair and unbiased compensation across all levels and roles. Our compensation structure is defined by job level (IC, Manager, Director, VP, C-Level) and is benchmarked against industry standards.

### 3.1. Average Compensation by Level

The following table presents the average total compensation (base salary + target bonus) for each job level in FY 2024.

| Job Level | FY 2024 Average Compensation (AED) |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Individual Contributor (IC)** | 294,000 |
| **Manager** | 441,000 |
| **Director** | 661,500 |
| **VP (Vice President)** | 1,102,500 |
| **C-Level** | 1,838,250 |

### 3.2. Pay Equity Findings

A preliminary analysis of the FY 2024 data, controlling for job level, department, and tenure, revealed a minor, statistically significant unadjusted pay gap of 3.1% favoring male employees. This gap is primarily concentrated in the Director and VP levels within the Engineering and Sales departments.

**Action Plan:**
1.  **Q1 2025:** Conduct a full, external-led pay equity audit to identify specific roles and individuals requiring adjustment.
2.  **Q2 2025:** Implement a **$1.5 million** equity adjustment pool to close identified gaps, prioritizing the most impacted groups.
3.  **Ongoing:** Integrate a "blind" compensation review process into all promotion and hiring decisions to mitigate unconscious bias.

